Redistributed in wwwroot/maps/<map>/*.svg
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Tarkov map SVGs   CC BY-NC-SA 4.0   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

  Original maps by Shebuka (https://github.com/the-hideout/tarkov-dev-svg-maps,
  https://github.com/TarkovTracker/tarkovdata). The per-floor layer files were
  prepared for SPT-DynamicMaps; some were modified by acidphantasm (Customs,
  Interchange, Woods) or dirtbikercj (Factory). The Labyrinth map is the work of
  acidphantasm. Those modifications are not made or endorsed by Shebuka.

  The expanded Interchange (wwwroot/maps/interchange-manimal/, shown only when
  the ManimalInterchange mod is loaded) comes from Interchange.svg in
  tarkov-dev-svg-maps (commit 6bbddad). QuestCodex split that single file into
  one file per floor (each keeps the original styles and one floor group); the
  drawing itself is unchanged.

  The Icebreaker decks (wwwroot/maps/icebreaker/, used for the location the
  ManimalIcebreaker mod adds) are adapted from re3mr's 2D Icebreaker map
  (https://reemr.se/, version 0.8, as published at
  https://tarkov.dev/maps/icebreaker-2d.jpg). QuestCodex cropped one panel per
  deck, removed the icons, labels and room names, and traced the rest into
  SVG (tools/maps/build-icebreaker-map.js). These adapted files are licensed
  under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 like the original (re3mr-LICENSE.md in that folder)
  and are not made or endorsed by re3mr.

  Apart from that split and the Icebreaker tracing, QuestCodex ships these files unmodified, as separate files, each map folder
  alongside its original license file (Shebuka-LICENSE*.md or
  acidphantasm-LICENSE.md, re3mr-LICENSE.md). The quest map popup credits the author, modifier
  and license of the map it shows. These files are not covered by LICENSE and
  may not be used commercially.


